                    <h2>About Octaria</h2>
                    <p>Octaria is an AI-native software agency based in Houston, Texas that has delivered custom software to small and mid-market companies since 2018. The firm builds with agents, runs on agents, and focuses on three areas: applied AI agents for business automation, internal AI operations (model selection and governance), and AI infrastructure cost management. I work with Octaria as a contract Software Applications Engineer, embedded on a long-running engagement for one of their clients&mdash;an energy investment firm.</p>

                    <hr class="major" />

                    <h2>About The Project</h2>
                    <p><strong>Mission:</strong> Build and operate a production AI agent platform for an energy investment firm&mdash;giving departments, crews, teams, and individual employees their own AI agents to help with everyday operations, research, and reporting. Because the firm works with highly sensitive deal and financial data, the platform had to make agents genuinely useful while guaranteeing at the network level that private data can never leave the company.</p>
                    <p><strong>Technologies Used:</strong> Anthropic Claude (Opus, Sonnet, Haiku), OpenClaw (Agent Runtime), Model Context Protocol (MCP) Servers, Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn, TanStack Query, Node.js, Python, AWS (EC2, S3, Systems Manager, Secrets Manager, DynamoDB, CloudWatch, WAF, Route 53), AWS CDK, Terraform, GitHub Actions (CI/CD), Microsoft Teams (Bot Framework), Microsoft Graph, Microsoft Entra ID, Slack, Squid (Egress Proxy), Tailscale (VPN), LanceDB (Vector Memory), Docker, Vitest, MkDocs Material (Technical Documentation), Claude Code (AI-Assisted Development with Custom Skills &amp; Commands), DocDD (Document-Driven Development).</p>
